msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "The process is in [LIP-1]{1}; in short:"
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Describe the problem in a discussion first."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Copy the [template]{1} to `docs/lips/lip-draft-<short-name>.md`, fill in every section, and open a change. The editors assign a number."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Move it to Review when the text is complete; it then goes to a 14-day Last Call and a decision by the Data Lead and the Technical Lead."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "An accepted LIP is recorded as a [decision record]{1} and released in a catalogue version."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Every LIP has a privacy and safeguarding section. The data this blueprint governs is mostly about children; say what your change does to it."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Setting up"
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Everything runs in the Nix dev shell, and every task is a `just` recipe, so your tools match everyone else's."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "With [direnv]{1}, `direnv allow` enters the shell for you."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Making the change"
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Edit the source, not the output.** Clause text, levels, verification and examples live in [`blueprint/catalogue.yaml`]{1}; standards in [`blueprint/standards.yaml`]{2}. Anything between `BEGIN GENERATED` and `END GENERATED` markers is written by `just render`; edit the source and run it."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Let the tools format.** Formatting and lint rules live in the configuration files at the root. Run `just fmt` rather than fixing layout by hand; if a rule is wrong, change the rule in its config file, in its own change."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Use the domain language.** Each bounded context's terms are in its `CONTEXT.md`, listed in the [context map]{1}. Use the canonical term, never a word under *Avoid*. A new term goes into its context's `CONTEXT.md` in the same change."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Write clauses that can be checked.** A clause uses MUST, SHOULD or MAY in the sense of [BCP 14]{1}, says what is required rather than which product provides it, and has a `verify` that a test or a reviewer can apply. Add an `example` when the clause is abstract."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Cite standards where they are published.** Link the publisher's own page for the edition you rely on, and add it to the standards register, rather than citing a summary of it."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Write English that translates well.** Short sentences, plain words, no text in images. After editing a page that has translations, run `just l10n-update` in the same change; see [translating]{1}."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "**Name roles, not people.** Write \"the Data Lead\", \"the steward of the learners domain\", never a person's name, and no real learners, staff or institutions in examples."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Committing"
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "The repository uses [jj]{1} colocated with Git; plain Git works too. Keep each change small and about one thing."
msgstr ""

#: CONTRIBUTING.md
msgid "Commit messages follow the Angular convention: `type(scope): subject`, with a lowercase, imperative subject under 72 characters, and a body that says *why*. Types are feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore and revert. Put `BREAKING CHANGE:` in the footer when a change breaks existing bindings."
msgstr ""

